#!/Applications/Xcode.app/Contents/Developer/Library/Frameworks/Python3.framework/Versions/3.9/bin/python3.9 -I
"""vpsrun — a human runs a queued play: every step shown, one phrase typed.

The agent writes a play (plays/*.yaml): an ordered list of vpsexec mutations
with a reason. The human types `vpsrun` in a real terminal, reads every step's
plan, types ONE phrase, and the steps run in order. The output lands in the
terminal and in the journal, where the agent reads it with `vpsexec last`.
Nothing is copied out of chat and nothing is pasted back in.

vpsrun holds no authority. Each step goes through the real `vpsexec` door
twice: once without --run to get its plan and plan-hash, then with
`--run --approve=<that hash>`. A step whose plan is break-glass also gets
`--approval-contract=FILE` (a grant from `vpsexec grant new`): --approve alone
no longer approves break-glass, so without a contract covering every
break-glass step the play refuses UP FRONT, before any step runs. With no
contract flag (or `--approval-contract=auto` / `--grant auto`) vpsrun picks ONE
grant for the whole play from those the door listed as valid for every
break-glass step's plan (short before reusable, then soonest-expiring, then
lowest id; a reusable one needs a use left per step; never a grant minted
`--for-release` for another release, and a play never picks one at all),
prints and journals it, and passes it explicitly to those steps (plain
vpsexec auto-picks only with --grant auto). Every gate (floor, secrets, posture, runbooks,
break-glass, locks, journal) runs exactly as for a hand-typed command. The
phrase replaces typing each step's own phrase; it does not replace any gate.

A step whose command is a READ is not planned (the door runs a read the moment
it is asked, plan mode included). It runs at its own position, after the
phrase, as a plain read: no --run, no --approve, no contract, and the door's
own output must say `tier    : read` or the play halts there.

Threats:
  - Protects against: a step changing between being shown and being run (the
    plan-hash binds hosts, order, command, containers and override; a mismatch
    refuses that step and halts the play); a play smuggling approval flags
    (--run, --approve, --reason and --yes are refused in a step's flags; only
    an allowlist passes); a read step running before approval or out of order
    (read steps are never sent to the door in plan mode; they run in place
    after the phrase), or a "read" step gaining authority (it is sent with no
    --run, --approve or contract, may carry only placement/timeout flags, and
    a door that does not report it as tier read halts the play — without
    --run the door runs nothing that is not a read); partial runs
    continuing blindly (first failure halts; later steps are listed as not run);
    a play failing halfway for want of break-glass approval (a contract's
    presence and its coverage of every break-glass step are checked before
    the play phrase is asked for).
  - Does NOT protect against: an agent that can already pass --approve itself.
    The TTY requirement keeps vpsrun a human tool; the boundary is still the
    door, not this file.

Releases, resume and the repeat guard (`vpsrun release NAME`, `--resume`):
a release (releases/NAME.yaml) is plays in order. Every step of every play is
planned and shown, and ONE phrase approves exactly those plans. Each run has
a run id, carried in every step's --reason and journaled (stream `vpsrun`)
per step. `--resume` continues the latest unfinished run of the same play or
release: a step whose exact plan already succeeded in that run is skipped,
everything else runs — except a step that reached the door. That one is
settled from the door's journal by the plan-hash its start recorded (never
its new plan): if it now plans differently, resume refuses ("changed after it
reached the door"); if its outcome is uncertain (lost contact, a retained
lock, or no mutation_complete at all), resume refuses and names `vpsexec
reconcile <host>` until each host is settled by a `reconciled` (or
`reconcile_free`) record — or, when the door died mid-way through a multi-host
attempt, by the door's own `host_done` record for that host (written only after
its every step, its verify and its lock release; a per-step record never
settles a host). Then, per host: completed (COMPLETED rc=0, verify passed or
none, or reported ok by the door) on EVERY host — not re-run by default: the
human types SKIP-DONE:<play>:<n> (journaled done, settled_from=reconcile|door,
the prompt naming per host which) or RERUN:<play>:<n>; completed on SOME hosts only —
only RERUN:<play>:<n> is accepted (the step runs again on all its hosts, the
completed ones named in the prompt), anything else refuses; completed nowhere
— it re-runs. A step whose door refusal is ONLY the identical-plan
guard, where every attempt the door saw in its window is this run's own
failed attempt at this very step, waits out the window with a countdown and
is retried once; any other run's identical plan still refuses.

A release re-plans each play at its boundary (after its hold) and asks a
REPLAN:<play>:... phrase over the new plan-hashes if any changed. A grant it
has the door mint is narrowed (--hosts, --max-uses = its break-glass steps),
bound --for-release, and revoked when the release completes. Refusals and
Ctrl-C reach the notifier too; a long step prints "still running" progress.

Threats (releases, resume, guard retry):
  - Protects against: resume re-running a non-idempotent step (a step is
    skipped only when the journal of THIS run says its exact plan-hash
    succeeded at that position, or a human typed SKIP-DONE over a reconcile
    that found it COMPLETED rc=0; a position that succeeded with a different
    plan refuses the resume rather than guess; an attempt whose outcome was
    never recorded is settled from the door's own journal by the plan-hash
    that attempt carried, and refuses when the door's journal cannot settle
    it, or when the step now plans differently); resume skipping a failed step
    (only `ok`/`skipped` records skip; a failed or unrecorded step runs);
    resume re-running an uncertain step blind (it refuses until reconcile has
    journaled every host); an unrelated reconcile settling a step (it must
    name the attempt's operation id or carry this step's run reason); a step
    that completed on some hosts being re-run there silently (mixed outcomes
    need an explicit RERUN naming those hosts);
    the guard retry laundering someone else's repeat (it fires only when the
    door's mutation_attempt records for this plan inside the window ALL carry
    this run's exact step reason and this run's journal shows that step
    failed; it waits the window out and asks the door again, so the door's
    guard still decides); one phrase approving plans it did not show (the
    phrase carries the count and a tag over exactly the plan-hashes that will
    run, and each step is run with its own --approve=<hash>); a conditional
    step matching its own command text (`when:` regexes see only the remote
    output block the door prints, not the plan).
  - Does NOT protect against: a same-user process editing the `vpsrun`
    journal stream to make resume skip a step (the stream is hash-chained and
    `vpscfg journal verify` detects it, but vpsrun does not verify the chain
    before every resume); plans that drift between being shown and being run
    because an EARLIER step changed live state (the door refuses the stale
    plan-hash and the release halts; --resume re-plans and asks again).
"""
import os
import sys

# Run isolated (-I): ignore every PYTHON* variable (PYTHONPATH, PYTHONHOME,
# PYTHONUSERBASE, PYTHONSTARTUP...), the user site-packages and the script's
# directory. Without it a sitecustomize.py on PYTHONPATH can patch
# Path.read_bytes in BOTH doors, so both obey a forged governor and the token
# still verifies (W4 review H1). The shebang names an ABSOLUTE interpreter with
# -I (`env python3` would let PATH pick a fake python3 that drops -I; W4 R1),
# so a door started by path is isolated from its first instruction. Public
# installs set the shebang to their own interpreter's absolute path. This
# re-exec only catches `python3 vpsrun`, which cannot be fully protected: a
# hostile startup hook in THAT first interpreter has run before this line.
# Callers must start the doors by path and deny the `python3 door` form.
# The shebang names the REAL interpreter binary (tools/pin-interpreter.sh):
# on macOS /usr/bin/python3 is an xcrun shim that honours DEVELOPER_DIR,
# TOOLCHAINS and SDKROOT, so it lets the environment pick the interpreter too.
# Every re-exec and child below uses _PYTHON, sys.executable resolved to its
# real file, and refuses a shim rather than run through one.


def _interpreter():
    exe = os.path.realpath(sys.executable or "")
    if not os.path.isabs(exe) or not os.path.isfile(exe) or (
            sys.platform == "darwin" and os.path.dirname(exe) == "/usr/bin"):
        sys.stderr.write("REFUSED: interpreter %r is not a real interpreter binary "
                         "(macOS /usr/bin entries are xcrun shims that honour "
                         "DEVELOPER_DIR); pin one with tools/pin-interpreter.sh\n"
                         % (sys.executable,))
        sys.exit(2)
    return exe


_PYTHON = _interpreter()

if __name__ == "__main__" and not sys.flags.isolated:
    os.execv(_PYTHON, [_PYTHON, "-I", os.path.realpath(__file__)] + sys.argv[1:])

import hashlib
import json
import re
import secrets
import shlex
import subprocess
import time
from pathlib import Path

REPO = Path(os.path.realpath(__file__)).parent
sys.path.insert(0, str(REPO))

# Queued plays name estate hosts, so they live under the estate root
# (vpscfg/estate.py: this checkout unless its pinned estate.path names another).
from vpscfg import estate as _estate  # noqa: E402

PLAY_DIR = _estate.root() / "plays"
RELEASE_DIR = _estate.root() / "releases"
# vpsrun's own per-step record of each run (resume reads it back).
RUN_STREAM = "vpsrun"
RUN_ID_RE = re.compile(r"^r_[0-9a-f]{16}$")
NAME_RE = re.compile(r"^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]{0,63}$")
STEP_ID_RE = re.compile(r"^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,32}$")
WHEN_RE = re.compile(r"^([A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,32}) reports (.+)$")
# The door's identical-plan refusal (vpsexec dispatch, gate 7b).
GUARD_TEXT = "Refusing an unattended repeat"
# A conditional step's regex sees at most this much remote output.
WHEN_MAX_CHARS = 1024 * 1024
VPSEXEC = [_PYTHON, "-I", str(REPO / "vpsexec")]
DIGEST_RE = re.compile(r"--approve=([0-9a-f]{64})\b")
# render_plan() prints these; vpsrun reads the door's own resolution of each
# step rather than re-deriving hosts or normalisation itself.
BREAK_GLASS_RE = re.compile(r"^\s*BREAK-GLASS: \d+ of \d+ host", re.M)
PLAN_HOSTS_RE = re.compile(r"^PLAN — \d+ hosts?: (.+)$", re.M)
PLAN_CMD_RE = re.compile(r"^  command : (.*)$", re.M)
# The door lists the VALID grants covering a break-glass plan (auto-pick
# order) under a `  grants  :` header; vpsrun only chooses among those ids and
# the door re-checks the chosen grant in full at every step.
GRANTS_HEAD = "  grants  : "
GRANT_LINE_RE = re.compile(
    r"^ {12}((?:st_|ru_)?[0-9a-f]{32}) (short|reusable) until "
    r"(\d{4}-\d\d-\d\dT\d\d:\d\d:\d\dZ) code ([A-Z2-7]{4}-[A-Z2-7]{4}-[A-Z2-7]{4})"
    r"(?: uses-left (\d+))?(?: release ([A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]{0,63}))?$")
KIND_ORDER = ("short", "reusable")  # narrower first, as the door ranks them
AUTO = "auto"  # `--approval-contract=auto` / `--grant auto`: same as omitting it
# Flags a step may carry. Approval, --run and --reason belong to vpsrun alone.
STEP_FLAGS = ("--override=", "--in=", "--in-match=", "--verify=", "--break-glass",
              "--canary", "--canary=", "--timeout=", "--require-blackout")
# A typed action (docs/ACTIONS.md) owns its placement and verify: --in=,
# --in-match= and --verify= are the door's own refusal there too.
ACTION_STEP_FLAGS = ("--override=", "--break-glass", "--canary", "--canary=",
                     "--timeout=", "--require-blackout")
# A read step has nothing to elevate, verify, canary or override.
READ_STEP_FLAGS = ("--in=", "--in-match=", "--timeout=")
# The FIRST tier line is the door's plan; anything later is remote output.
TIER_RE = re.compile(r"^  tier    : (.*)$", re.M)
PLAY_KEYS = {"version", "reason", "steps", "precheck"}
# Named read-only audits a play may demand before anything is planned. Each
# runs through the real vpscfg door against every host the play touches;
# a non-zero exit (any CRITICAL/HIGH finding) refuses the whole play.
PRECHECKS = {"k3s": ["fleet", "k3s"], "firewall": ["fleet", "firewall"]}
VPSCFG = [_PYTHON, "-I", str(REPO / "vpscfg-control.py")]
# Any control character (C0, DEL, C1) in text shown to the approving human
# could clear the screen or rewrite a plan already printed. Refused at load.
CONTROL_RE = re.compile(r"[\x00-\x1f\x7f-\x9f]")
STEP_KEYS = {"hosts", "cmd", "why", "flags", "push", "sha256", "id", "when",
             "action", "with"}
# A `with:` JSON object the door's own --with ceiling accepts (docs/ACTIONS.md).
WITH_JSON_MAX = 8192
ACTION_NAME_RE = re.compile(r"^[a-z][a-z0-9_]{0,31}(?:@[1-9][0-9]{0,5})?$")
SHA_RE = re.compile(r"^[0-9a-f]{64}$")
# The door names the release valve when a step retains or meets a held lock.
RECONCILE_RE = re.compile(r"vpsexec reconcile ([A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]*)")


class Refused(Exception):
    pass


def _clean(where, value):
    value = str(value)
    if CONTROL_RE.search(value):
        raise Refused("%s contains a control character %r — refused: it could "
                      "redraw the terminal the approver is reading"
                      % (where, CONTROL_RE.search(value).group(0)))
    return value


def printable(text):
    """Plan text comes from the door, which echoes the command. Escape every
    control character except newline before it reaches the approver's screen."""
    return "".join(c if c == "\n" or not CONTROL_RE.match(c)
                   else "\\x%02x" % ord(c) for c in text)


def load_play(path):
    import yaml
    raw = Path(path).read_bytes()
    doc = yaml.safe_load(raw)
    if not isinstance(doc, dict) or doc.get("version") != 1:
        raise Refused("%s: not a version-1 play" % path)
    unknown = sorted(set(doc) - PLAY_KEYS)
    if unknown:
        raise Refused("%s: unknown key(s) %r" % (path, unknown))
    reason = _clean("reason", doc.get("reason") or "").strip()
    if not reason:
        raise Refused("%s: a play needs a reason — it is journaled on every step" % path)
    steps = doc.get("steps")
    if not isinstance(steps, list) or not steps:
        raise Refused("%s: steps must be a non-empty list" % path)
    out = []
    for n, s in enumerate(steps, 1):
        if not isinstance(s, dict):
            raise Refused("step %d is not a mapping" % n)
        unknown = sorted(set(s) - STEP_KEYS)
        if unknown:
            raise Refused("step %d: unknown key(s) %r" % (n, unknown))
        is_push = "push" in s
        is_action = "action" in s or "with" in s
        if sum((is_push, is_action, "cmd" in s)) > 1:
            raise Refused("step %d: exactly one of cmd:, push: or action:+with:" % n)
        if is_push and ("cmd" in s or not SHA_RE.match(str(s.get("sha256", "")))):
            raise Refused("step %d: a push step names push + sha256 (64 hex) and no cmd" % n)
        if not is_push and "sha256" in s:
            raise Refused("step %d: sha256 belongs to a push step" % n)
        if is_action:
            action_name = _clean("step %d action" % n, s.get("action") or "")
            if not ACTION_NAME_RE.match(action_name):
                raise Refused("step %d: action %r must be [a-z][a-z0-9_]{0,31}, "
                              "optionally @VERSION" % (n, action_name))
            with_value = s.get("with", {}) if "with" in s else {}
            if with_value is None:
                with_value = {}
            if not isinstance(with_value, dict):
                raise Refused("step %d: with: must be a mapping, not %s"
                              % (n, type(with_value).__name__))
            if len(json.dumps(with_value)) > WITH_JSON_MAX:
                raise Refused("step %d: with: is over %d bytes" % (n, WITH_JSON_MAX))
        key = "push" if is_push else ("action" if is_action else "cmd")
        for req in ("hosts", key, "why"):
            if not str(s.get(req) or "").strip():
                raise Refused("step %d: missing %r" % (n, req))
            _clean("step %d %s" % (n, req), s[req])
        if not is_push and not is_action:
            from vpscfg import actions
            if actions.is_reserved(s["cmd"]):
                raise Refused(str(actions.reserved_refusal("step %d cmd" % n)))
        flags = [_clean("step %d flag" % n, f) for f in (s.get("flags") or [])]
        allowed_flags = ACTION_STEP_FLAGS if is_action else STEP_FLAGS
        for f in flags:
            if not any(f == allowed or (allowed.endswith("=") and f.startswith(allowed))
                       for allowed in allowed_flags):
                raise Refused("step %d: flag %r is not allowed in a %sstep (allowed: %s)"
                              % (n, f, "typed-action " if is_action else "",
                                 ", ".join(allowed_flags)))
        if is_push:
            out.append({"hosts": str(s["hosts"]), "push": str(s["push"]),
                        "sha256": str(s["sha256"]), "why": str(s["why"]), "flags": flags,
                        "cmd": "push %s" % s["push"]})
        elif is_action:
            out.append({"hosts": str(s["hosts"]), "action": action_name,
                        "with": with_value, "why": str(s["why"]), "flags": flags})
        else:
            out.append({"hosts": str(s["hosts"]), "cmd": str(s["cmd"]),
                        "why": str(s["why"]), "flags": flags})
        _step_condition(out, n, s)
    precheck = doc.get("precheck") or []
    if not isinstance(precheck, list) or any(p not in PRECHECKS for p in precheck):
        raise Refused("%s: precheck must be a list drawn from %s" % (path, sorted(PRECHECKS)))
    return {"path": str(path), "sha256": hashlib.sha256(raw).hexdigest(),
            "reason": reason, "steps": out, "precheck": list(precheck)}


def _step_condition(out, n, raw):
    """`id:` names a step; `when: "<earlier id> reports <regex>"` makes a step
    optional: it runs only if that earlier step's remote output matches."""
    step = out[-1]
    if "id" in raw:
        sid = _clean("step %d id" % n, raw["id"])
        if not STEP_ID_RE.match(sid):
            raise Refused("step %d: id %r must be 1-32 of [A-Za-z0-9_-]" % (n, sid))
        if any(o.get("id") == sid for o in out[:-1]):
            raise Refused("step %d: id %r is already used by an earlier step" % (n, sid))
        step["id"] = sid
    if "when" in raw:
        text = _clean("step %d when" % n, raw["when"]).strip()
        m = WHEN_RE.match(text)
        if not m:
            raise Refused("step %d: when must read '<earlier step id> reports <regex>'" % n)
        ref = [k for k, o in enumerate(out[:-1], 1) if o.get("id") == m.group(1)]
        if not ref:
            raise Refused("step %d: when names %r, which is not the id of an EARLIER "
                          "step in this play" % (n, m.group(1)))
        try:
            re.compile(m.group(2))
        except re.error as e:
            raise Refused("step %d: when regex %r does not compile (%s)" % (n, m.group(2), e))
        step["when"] = {"id": m.group(1), "step": ref[0], "regex": m.group(2)}


def remote_output(out):
    """Only what the hosts printed: the block between the door's first
    `───── host ─────` header and its last `SUMMARY — ` line. The plan above
    it echoes the command, so a regex must never see it."""
    lines = out.splitlines()
    start = [i for i, l in enumerate(lines) if l.startswith("───── ")]
    if not start:
        return ""
    end = [i for i, l in enumerate(lines) if l.startswith("SUMMARY — ")]
    stop = end[-1] if end and end[-1] > start[0] else len(lines)
    body = [l for l in lines[start[0]:stop] if not l.startswith("───── ")]
    return "\n".join(body)[:WHEN_MAX_CHARS]


def read_steps(play, classify=None):
    """Step numbers whose command is a read.

    Plan mode RUNS a read, so a read step must never be planned: it runs in
    place after the phrase, as a plain read (see run_play). Its flags are
    limited to placement and timeout, because nothing else means anything for
    a read and a read step must not carry anything that looks like authority."""
    if classify is None:
        from vpscfg import gates, vpsexec
        classify = lambda c: vpsexec.classify(c, gates.DENY_ALWAYS_FLOOR)[0]  # noqa: E731
    reads = set()
    for n, s in enumerate(play["steps"], 1):
        if "push" in s:
            continue  # always a mutation; vpsexec checks the file and its hash
        if "action" in s:
            # The tier is fixed in code per action (docs/ACTIONS.md): no host
            # or param data changes it, so this needs no host and no door call.
            from vpscfg import actions
            try:
                tier = actions.get(s["action"], "step").tier
            except Exception as e:
                raise Refused("step %d refused: %s" % (n, e))
        else:
            try:
                tier = classify(s["cmd"])
            except Exception as e:  # refused outright: say so now, not mid-play
                raise Refused("step %d refused by the classifier: %s" % (n, e))
        if tier == "read":
            label = s.get("cmd") or "action %s" % s["action"]
            extra = [f for f in s["flags"] if not f.startswith(READ_STEP_FLAGS)]
            if extra:
                raise Refused("step %d (%s) is a read; a read step may carry only "
                              "%s, not %s" % (n, label, ", ".join(READ_STEP_FLAGS),
                                              ", ".join(extra)))
            reads.add(n)
    return reads


def read_tag(play, n, step, run_id=None):
    """Stands in for a plan-hash in the play phrase: binds the read as shown."""
    return hashlib.sha256(("read\0" + "\0".join(step_argv(play, n, step, run_id)))
                          .encode("utf-8")).hexdigest()


def step_reason(play, n, step, run_id=None):
    """The run id rides in the reason, so the door's own journal says which
    run made each attempt (the guard-aware retry reads it back)."""
    base = "%s — step %d: %s" % (play["reason"], n, step["why"])
    return "%s [run %s]" % (base, run_id) if run_id else base


def step_argv(play, n, step, run_id=None):
    """The same argv for planning and running; vpsexec wants --reason in both.

    An action step hands the door `--action NAME --with JSON`: vpsrun never
    builds the body itself (docs/ACTIONS.md), only the typed literals the
    policy's play step already carries."""
    if "push" in step:
        head = [step["hosts"], "push", step["push"], "--sha256", step["sha256"]]
    elif "action" in step:
        head = [step["hosts"], "--action", step["action"], "--with",
                json.dumps(step["with"], sort_keys=True, separators=(",", ":"))]
    else:
        head = [step["hosts"], step["cmd"]]
    return head + step["flags"] + ["--reason", step_reason(play, n, step, run_id)]


def plan_all(play, run, reads=(), run_id=None):
    """Plan every step through the real door. Returns [(plan_text, digest)].
    A read step is NOT sent to the door here (it would run now)."""
    plans = []
    for n, s in enumerate(play["steps"], 1):
        if n in reads:
            plans.append(("READ — runs here, after approval, as a plain read (no "
                          "--run, no approval, no contract):\n  vpsexec %s"
                          % " ".join(shlex.quote(a) for a in step_argv(play, n, s)[:-2]),
                          read_tag(play, n, s, run_id)))
            continue
        rc, out = run(step_argv(play, n, s, run_id))
        found = DIGEST_RE.findall(out)
        if rc != 0 or len(set(found)) != 1:
            raise Refused("step %d did not produce a plan (rc=%s):\n%s" % (n, rc, out))
        plans.append((out, found[0]))
    return plans


def phrase(play, digests=()):
    """Step count, break-glass count, and 6 hex of the plans shown: typing it
    approves THESE plans, not any play of the same length."""
    return run_phrase("PLAY", play["steps"], digests)


def run_phrase(prefix, steps, digests=()):
    """`<prefix>:<steps>[:BREAK-GLASS:<n>][:<tag>]` over the steps that will run."""
    bg = sum(1 for s in steps if "--break-glass" in s["flags"])
    tag = hashlib.sha256("".join(digests).encode()).hexdigest()[:6] if digests else ""
    return "%s:%d%s%s" % (prefix, len(steps), ":BREAK-GLASS:%d" % bg if bg else "",
                          ":" + tag if tag else "")


def run_prechecks(play, check):
    """Every precheck must pass on every host the play touches, before any
    step is planned. `check(argv) -> (rc, output)` runs vpscfg."""
    hosts = []
    for s in play["steps"]:
        for h in s["hosts"].split(","):
            if h and not h.startswith("@") and h not in hosts:
                hosts.append(h)
    for name in play.get("precheck", []):
        rc, text = check(PRECHECKS[name] + hosts)
        print(text.rstrip())
        if rc != 0:
            raise Refused("precheck %r failed on %s — nothing was planned or run. Fix what "
                          "it reports, then re-run the play." % (name, ", ".join(hosts)))


def door_grants(text):
    """{session_id: {kind, until, code, left}} from the door's plan for one
    step: the grants it found VALID for that exact plan. Only the block under
    the door's own header is read."""
    lines = text.splitlines()
    heads = [i for i, l in enumerate(lines) if l.startswith(GRANTS_HEAD)]
    found = {}
    if not heads:
        return found
    for line in lines[heads[0] + 1:]:
        m = GRANT_LINE_RE.match(line)
        if not m:
            break
        found[m.group(1)] = {"session_id": m.group(1), "kind": m.group(2),
                             "until": m.group(3), "code": m.group(4),
                             "left": None if m.group(5) is None else int(m.group(5)),
                             "release": m.group(6)}
    return found


def _short_id(sid):
    return sid[:11] if sid[2:3] == "_" else sid[:8]


def auto_pick(play, plans, bg, grant_dir=None, release=None):
    """ONE grant for the whole play: valid for every break-glass step's exact
    plan (as the door judged each), with enough uses left for all of them.
    Narrower kind first, then soonest-expiring, then lowest id. A grant minted
    --for-release is picked only by that release (M6): a play or another
    release never spends its uses. Returns (absolute path, info), or None when
    nothing covers every step."""
    per_step = [door_grants(plans[n - 1][0]) for n in bg]
    common = set(per_step[0]).intersection(*per_step[1:])
    ok = []
    for sid in common:
        info = dict(per_step[0][sid])
        if info.get("release") != release and info.get("release") is not None:
            continue
        if info["kind"] == "reusable":
            left = min(ps[sid]["left"] if ps[sid]["left"] is not None else -1
                       for ps in per_step)
            if left < len(bg):
                continue
            info["left"] = left
        ok.append(info)
    if not ok:
        return None
    ok.sort(key=lambda i: (KIND_ORDER.index(i["kind"]), i["until"], i["session_id"]))
    chosen = ok[0]
    chosen["ties"] = [i["session_id"] for i in ok[1:]
                      if (i["kind"], i["until"]) == (chosen["kind"], chosen["until"])]
    if grant_dir is None:
        from vpscfg import vpsexecgrant
        grant_dir = vpsexecgrant.GRANT_DIR
    return str(Path(grant_dir) / ("%s.json" % chosen["session_id"])), chosen


def contract_coverage(play, plans, contract, load_grant=None):
    """Break-glass step numbers, after refusing anything a contract would not
    cover. Runs before the play is approved, so a play never fails halfway on
    a missing approval."""
    bg = [n for n, (text, _) in enumerate(plans, 1) if BREAK_GLASS_RE.search(text)]
    if not bg:
        return bg
    if contract is None:
        raise Refused(
            "step(s) %s are break-glass, and --approve alone no longer approves "
            "break-glass, and no valid grant in ~/.vpscfg/grants covers all of "
            "them. Mint one (vpsexec grant new <runbook> --ttl <ttl> --run, or "
            "--kind reusable), then re-run: vpsrun %s. Nothing was run."
            % (", ".join(map(str, bg)), play["path"]))
    if load_grant is None:
        from vpscfg import gates, vpsexecgrant

        def load_grant(path):
            try:
                return vpsexecgrant.preflight(path)
            except gates.Refused as r:
                raise Refused(str(r))
    grant = load_grant(contract)
    if grant.get("kind") == "reusable":
        # No step list to compare: the door judged each plan against the
        # policy as loaded now and listed the grants that cover it.
        sid = grant["session_id"]
        listed = [door_grants(plans[n - 1][0]).get(sid) for n in bg]
        uncovered = [n for n, info in zip(bg, listed) if info is None]
        if uncovered:
            raise Refused("reusable grant %s does not cover break-glass step(s) %s "
                          "(the door did not list it as valid for those plans). "
                          "Nothing was run." % (contract, ", ".join(map(str, uncovered))))
        left = min(info["left"] if info["left"] is not None else -1 for info in listed)
        if left < len(bg):
            raise Refused("reusable grant %s has %d use(s) left; this play needs %d "
                          "(one per break-glass step). Nothing was run."
                          % (contract, max(left, 0), len(bg)))
        return bg
    covered = set((st["cmd"], st["where"]) for st in grant["steps"])
    uncovered = []
    for n in bg:
        text, step = plans[n - 1][0], play["steps"][n - 1]
        cmd = PLAN_CMD_RE.search(text)
        hosts = PLAN_HOSTS_RE.search(text)
        where = ("container" if any(f.startswith(("--in=", "--in-match="))
                                    for f in step["flags"]) else "host")
        if (not cmd or not hosts or (cmd.group(1), where) not in covered
                or not set(h.strip() for h in hosts.group(1).split(","))
                <= set(grant["hosts"])):
            uncovered.append(n)
    if uncovered:
        raise Refused("approval contract %s does not cover break-glass step(s) %s "
                      "(command, placement or hosts) — mint a grant that does. "
                      "Nothing was run." % (contract, ", ".join(map(str, uncovered))))
    return bg


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# runs: one run id per play or release, journaled per step (stream `vpsrun`)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

def new_run_id():
    return "r_" + secrets.token_hex(8)


def _rjournal(entry):
    """Journal-or-refuse: a step whose start cannot be recorded does not run,
    because resume could not tell later whether it had."""
    from vpscfg import journal
    journal.append(RUN_STREAM, entry)


def _run_records(run_id=None):
    from vpscfg import vpsexeclog
    try:
        recs = vpsexeclog.read(RUN_STREAM)
    except Exception as e:
        raise Refused("journal stream %s unreadable (%s) — refusing to guess what "
                      "already ran" % (RUN_STREAM, e))
    if any(r.get("event") == "_unparseable" for r in recs):
        raise Refused("journal stream %s has unparseable lines — resume cannot trust "
                      "it; run `vpscfg journal verify`" % RUN_STREAM)
    return [r for r in recs if run_id is None or r.get("run_id") == run_id]


def find_resumable(kind, name):
    """The latest run of this play or release, which must not have completed."""
    starts = [r for r in _run_records() if r.get("event") == "run_started"
              and r.get("kind") == kind and r.get("name") == name]
    if not starts:
        raise Refused("no earlier run of %s %s to resume — run it without --resume"
                      % (kind, name))
    run_id = str(starts[-1].get("run_id"))
    if not RUN_ID_RE.match(run_id):
        raise Refused("the latest run of %s %s has a malformed run id %r" % (kind, name, run_id))
    if any(r.get("event") == "run_complete" for r in _run_records(run_id)):
        raise Refused("the latest run (%s) of %s %s completed — nothing to resume. "
                      "Run it again without --resume for a new run." % (run_id, kind, name))
    return run_id


def _key(play):
    return os.path.realpath(play["path"])


def _play_name(play):
    return Path(play["path"]).stem


def prepare(plays, run, run_id, check=None, prechecks=True):
    """Plan every step of every play through the door (reads are not planned).
    One unit per step, in run order."""
    units = []
    for play in plays:
        if prechecks and play.get("precheck"):
            run_prechecks(play, check or _vpscfg_run)
        reads = read_steps(play)
        plans = plan_all(play, run, reads, run_id)
        for n, (text, digest) in enumerate(plans, 1):
            units.append({"play": play, "n": n, "step": play["steps"][n - 1],
                          "text": text, "digest": digest, "read": n in reads,
                          "done": None, "reports": {}})
    return units


def _door_outcome(u, run_id, started):
    """A step whose start is journaled but whose end is not (vpsrun was killed,
    the terminal closed). The door's own journal settles it: no attempt with
    this run's reason and plan-hash since the start => it never reached the
    door; an attempt and its mutation_complete => that outcome; an attempt and
    nothing after it => `unknown`, which _check_uncertain settles only through
    `vpsexec reconcile`.

    The door's journal is searched by the plan-hash THIS start recorded (and
    the run-scoped reason), never by the step's new plan: a step that reached
    the door and now plans differently refuses ("changed after it reached the
    door") instead of being settled, or re-run, under another plan."""
    from vpscfg import vpsexeclog
    recs = vpsexeclog.read()
    reason = step_reason(u["play"], u["n"], u["step"], run_id)
    digest = started.get("digest")
    idx = _attempts(recs, digest, reason)
    started_age = vpsexeclog.age_seconds(started)
    if not idx or started_age is None:
        return None
    attempt = recs[idx[-1]]
    attempt_age = vpsexeclog.age_seconds(attempt)
    if attempt_age is None or attempt_age > started_age + 1:
        return None  # only an older attempt: this start never reached the door
    _refuse_if_changed(u, run_id, digest)
    j = _complete_after(recs, idx[-1])
    if j is None:
        return {"status": "unknown", "digest": digest, "reports": {}}
    done = recs[j]
    ok = not done.get("failed") and not done.get("not_run")
    return {"status": "ok" if ok else "failed", "digest": digest, "reports": {}}


def _attempts(recs, digest, reason):
    return [i for i, r in enumerate(recs) if r.get("event") == "mutation_attempt"
            and r.get("plan_hash") == digest and r.get("reason") == reason]


def _complete_after(recs, i):
    """Index of the attempt's own mutation_complete, or None."""
    a = recs[i]
    for j in range(i + 1, len(recs)):
        r = recs[j]
        if (r.get("event") == "mutation_complete" and r.get("command") == a.get("command")
                and r.get("hosts") == a.get("hosts")):
            return j
    return None


def _refuse_if_changed(u, run_id, digest):
    if digest != u["digest"]:
        raise Refused(
            "%s step %d changed after it reached the door in run %s: it ran (or may "
            "have run) as plan %s and now plans as %s. Resume will not settle or re-run "
            "it under a different plan. Check what it did (vpsexec last), restore the "
            "play or the state it planned against, or start a fresh run without "
            "--resume." % (_play_name(u["play"]), u["n"], run_id, str(digest)[:12],
                           u["digest"][:12]))


def _uncertain_ops(u, run_id, recs, digest):
    """What the door left UNCERTAIN for this step in this run, as a list of
    {host, op, attempt}: a detached step that lost contact (a `step` record
    with `uncertain`), a host whose lock it retained (`lock_retained` on
    mutation_complete), or — when an attempt has NO mutation_complete at all
    (Ctrl-C, a dropped terminal) — every host of that attempt, with the
    operation id its `step` records carry, if any. Searched by `digest`, the
    plan-hash the run recorded, and the run-scoped reason. Every attempt of
    the step in this run counts, not only the last one."""
    reason = step_reason(u["play"], u["n"], u["step"], run_id)
    found = []
    for i in _attempts(recs, digest, reason):
        hosts = recs[i].get("hosts") or []
        j = _complete_after(recs, i)
        window = recs[i + 1:j if j is not None else len(recs)]
        steps = [r for r in window if r.get("event") == "step" and r.get("host") in hosts]
        if j is None:
            for h in hosts:
                mine = [r for r in steps if r.get("host") == h]
                ops = [r.get("operation_id") for r in mine if r.get("operation_id")]
                e = {"host": h, "op": ops[-1] if ops else None, "attempt": i}
                # A host the door FINISHED before it died is settled by the
                # door's own `host_done` record — written only after every
                # step, the verify and the lock release (its lock is free, so
                # a reconcile could only say so). A per-step record proves
                # nothing: the door may have died between container steps or
                # during the verify, with the lock still held.
                # Only THIS attempt's host_done: it carries the attempt's
                # run-scoped reason and plan-hash, and it is searched only up
                # to the next mutation_attempt that reaches this host (a later
                # operation's host_done never counts).
                stop = next((k for k, r in enumerate(window)
                             if r.get("event") == "mutation_attempt"
                             and h in (r.get("hosts") or [])), len(window))
                done = [r for r in window[:stop] if r.get("event") == "host_done"
                        and r.get("host") == h and r.get("reason") == reason
                        and r.get("plan_hash") == digest
                        and (not e["op"] or r.get("operation_id") == e["op"])]
                if done:
                    d = done[-1]
                    e["op"] = e["op"] or d.get("operation_id")
                    e["settled"] = {"event": "finished", "host": h, "verdict": "COMPLETED",
                                    "rc": d.get("rc"), "verify_rc": d.get("verify_rc"),
                                    "already_done": bool(d.get("already_done"))}
                found.append(e)
            continue
        for r in steps:
            if r.get("uncertain"):
                found.append({"host": r["host"], "op": r.get("operation_id"), "attempt": i})
        for h, op in sorted((recs[j].get("lock_retained") or {}).items()):
            found.append({"host": h, "op": op, "attempt": i})
    out = []
    for e in found:
        if all((e["host"], e["op"]) != (o["host"], o["op"]) for o in out):
            out.append(e)
    return out, reason


def _settlement(e, recs, reason):
    """The `vpsexec reconcile` record that settles one uncertain entry: a
    `reconciled` record after the attempt for that host whose operation id is
    the entry's, or — when no op id was journaled — whose lock owner carries
    this run's step reason; or a `reconcile_free` record (the lock was already
    free when a human looked). For a KNOWN op, a free lock with no host_done
    means the door released it and died before journaling the outcome: it is
    settled as RELEASED, OUTCOME UNKNOWN, which never counts as completed (the
    step runs again; never SKIP-DONE). None if open."""
    for r in recs[e["attempt"] + 1:]:
        if r.get("host") != e["host"]:
            continue
        if r.get("event") == "reconciled" and (
                (e["op"] and r.get("operation_id") == e["op"])
                or (not e["op"] and (r.get("owner") or {}).get("reason") == reason)):
            return r
        if r.get("event") == "reconcile_free":
            if not e["op"]:
                return r
            # A known op whose lock is free with no host_done: the door
            # released it and died before journaling the outcome (or that
            # write failed). Released by the door, outcome UNKNOWN: it runs
            # again (never SKIP-DONE).
            return dict(r, verdict="RELEASED, OUTCOME UNKNOWN")
    return None


def _completed_ok(s):
    return (s.get("event") in ("reconciled", "finished") and s.get("verdict") == "COMPLETED"
            and s.get("rc") == 0 and s.get("verify_rc") in (None, 0))


def _host_outcomes(entries, recs):
    """(done, not_done): the step's hosts split by whether the step provably
    completed there — reconciled or finished COMPLETED rc=0 with its verify
    passing (or none), or a host the door itself reported successful."""
    done, not_done = [], []

    def add(lst, h):
        if h not in done and h not in not_done:
            lst.append(h)
    for e in entries:
        add(done if _completed_ok(e["settled"]) else not_done, e["host"])
    for i in set(e["attempt"] for e in entries):
        j = _complete_after(recs, i)
        if j is None:
            continue  # every host of an attempt with no outcome is an entry
        failed = set(recs[j].get("failed") or []) | set(recs[j].get("not_run") or [])
        for h in recs[i].get("hosts") or []:
            add(not_done if h in failed else done, h)
    return done, not_done


def _check_uncertain(u, run_id, digest, ask=None):
    """A failed or unknown step whose outcome the door could not establish is
    neither done nor safely failed. Resume refuses it until `vpsexec reconcile
    <host>` has journaled each host; the refusal names the command.

    A `reconciled` record outranks the door's host_done; a known op whose lock
    a reconcile found free with no host_done is RELEASED, OUTCOME UNKNOWN
    (not completed). Settled: when the step provably completed on EVERY host (reconciled
    COMPLETED rc=0, or finished by the door — its host_done record, written
    only after the verify and the lock release — with rc=0; verify passed or
    none), it is NOT re-run by default: the human types SKIP-DONE:<play>:<n>
    (journaled done, settled_from=reconcile|door) or RERUN:<play>:<n>; anything
    else refuses. The prompt says, per host, which evidence it rests on. When it
    completed on SOME hosts only, resume cannot re-run it on the others alone:
    it asks for an explicit RERUN:<play>:<n> (the step runs again on ALL its
    hosts, the completed ones named), anything else refuses. When it completed
    nowhere it runs again through the door, never counted as done.
    Returns True when the step is now settled done."""
    from vpscfg import vpsexeclog
    recs = vpsexeclog.read()
    entries, reason = _uncertain_ops(u, run_id, recs, digest)
    if not entries:
        return False
    _refuse_if_changed(u, run_id, digest)
    for e in entries:
        # A reconcile that inspected the host outranks the door's host_done.
        rec = _settlement(e, recs, reason)
        if e.get("settled") is None or (rec and rec.get("event") == "reconciled"):
            e["settled"] = rec if rec is not None else e.get("settled")
    open_hosts = []
    for e in entries:
        if e["settled"] is None and e["host"] not in open_hosts:
            open_hosts.append(e["host"])
    if open_hosts:
        raise Refused(
            "%s step %d's outcome is UNCERTAIN in run %s (it reached the door, and the "
            "door lost contact or its outcome was never recorded; a lock may be "
            "retained on %s). Resume refuses to guess: it neither skips it nor runs it "
            "blind. Next, a human runs, in a terminal:\n%s\nthen resume again."
            % (_play_name(u["play"]), u["n"], run_id, ", ".join(open_hosts),
               "\n".join("  vpsexec reconcile %s" % h for h in open_hosts)))
    for e in entries:
        s = e["settled"]
        print("  %s step %d: uncertain on %s, %s (verdict %s%s)"
              % (_play_name(u["play"]), u["n"], e["host"],
                 "finished before the door died" if s.get("event") == "finished"
                 else "reconciled",
                 s.get("verdict") or "lock free",
                 "" if s.get("rc") is None else " rc=%s" % s.get("rc")))
    name = _play_name(u["play"])
    skip, rerun = "SKIP-DONE:%s:%d" % (name, u["n"]), "RERUN:%s:%d" % (name, u["n"])
    done, not_done = _host_outcomes(entries, recs)
    if not done:
        print("    — it runs again through the door, not counted as done.")
        return False
    # A typed action's idempotent check settles this on its own (S7: the check
    # never released the lock — the door had already finished and released it
    # before it died). The check already proved every host done; there is
    # nothing for a human to decide, so no SKIP-DONE/RERUN phrase is asked.
    if not not_done and all(e["settled"].get("event") == "finished"
                            and e["settled"].get("already_done") for e in entries):
        print("    [done] %s — settled by the action's own check, no phrase needed"
              % ", ".join(done))
        _rjournal({"event": "step_done", "run_id": run_id, "play": _key(u["play"]),
                   "step": u["n"], "digest": u["digest"], "status": "ok", "rc": 0,
                   "settled_from": "check", "operations": [e["op"] for e in entries],
                   "reports": {}})
        return True
    caution = _rerun_caution(u["step"])
    if caution:
        print("    CAUTION: %s" % caution)
    if not_done:
        if ask is None:
            raise Refused("%s step %d completed on %s but not on %s; resuming needs a "
                          "human at a terminal to type %s" % (name, u["n"], ", ".join(done),
                                                              ", ".join(not_done), rerun))
        answer = ask("%s step %d COMPLETED on %s but not on %s. Resume cannot run it on "
                     "some of its hosts only. Type %s to run it again on ALL its hosts "
                     "(including %s), anything else aborts: "
                     % (name, u["n"], ", ".join(done), ", ".join(not_done), rerun,
                        ", ".join(done))).strip()
        if answer != rerun:
            raise Refused("%s was not typed — nothing ran. To finish only %s, run that "
                          "step by hand through vpsexec, then start a fresh run."
                          % (rerun, ", ".join(not_done)))
        print("    — it runs again through the door on all its hosts, not counted as done.")
        return False
    # Say where each host's COMPLETED comes from: only a host a `vpsexec
    # reconcile` actually inspected is "reconciled"; one the door itself
    # finished (host_done) is "finished by the door".
    sources = sorted(set("reconcile" if e["settled"].get("event") == "reconciled"
                         else "door" for e in entries))
    evidence = "; ".join(
        "%s: %s" % (e["host"], "reconciled COMPLETED rc=0"
                    if e["settled"].get("event") == "reconciled"
                    else "finished by the door (host_done rc=0)") for e in entries)
    if ask is None:
        raise Refused("%s step %d COMPLETED rc=0 on every host (%s); resuming needs a "
                      "human at a terminal to type %s or %s"
                      % (name, u["n"], evidence, skip, rerun))
    answer = ask("%s step %d COMPLETED rc=0 on every host (%s). Type %s to count it done, "
                 "or %s to run it again; anything else aborts: "
                 % (name, u["n"], evidence, skip, rerun)).strip()
    if answer == rerun:
        print("    — it runs again through the door, not counted as done.")
        return False
    if answer != skip:
        raise Refused("neither %s nor %s was typed — nothing ran" % (skip, rerun))
    _rjournal({"event": "step_done", "run_id": run_id, "play": _key(u["play"]),
               "step": u["n"], "digest": u["digest"], "status": "ok", "rc": 0,
               "settled_from": "+".join(sources),
               "operations": [e["op"] for e in entries], "reports": {}})
    return True


def _rerun_caution(step):
    """What a RERUN repeats that a human should know before typing it (L4):
    `migrate` is not idempotent, and its `sql_dir` runner applies EVERY .sql
    file again, including the ones that already succeeded (it keeps no
    record of applied files; the other runners' own tools usually do)."""
    if step.get("action", "").split("@", 1)[0] != "migrate":
        return None
    if (step.get("with") or {}).get("runner") == "sql_dir":
        return ("RERUN of migrate (runner sql_dir) applies every .sql file in its workdir "
                "AGAIN, including the ones that already succeeded — only type RERUN if "
                "each file is safe to apply twice; otherwise SKIP-DONE and finish by hand")
    return ("RERUN of migrate runs the project's migration tool again; it is safe only "
            "if that tool skips migrations it already applied")


def resume_plan(units, run_id, ask=None):
    """Mark each unit done from THIS run's journal. Only an `ok` or `skipped`
    record with the same plan-hash at the same position skips a step; a
    position that succeeded under a different plan refuses the resume.
    `ask(msg) -> str` is the TTY prompt used to settle a reconciled step."""
    last = {}
    for r in _run_records(run_id):
        if r.get("event") in ("step_started", "step_done"):
            last[(r.get("play"), r.get("step"))] = r
    for u in units:
        rec = last.get((_key(u["play"]), u["n"]))
        if rec is None:
            continue
        if rec.get("event") == "step_started":
            if u["read"]:
                continue  # a read is safe to repeat
            rec = _door_outcome(u, run_id, rec)
            if rec is None:
                continue
            if rec["status"] != "unknown":
                _rjournal({"event": "step_done", "run_id": run_id,
                           "play": _key(u["play"]), "step": u["n"],
                           "digest": rec["digest"], "status": rec["status"],
                           "rc": 0 if rec["status"] == "ok" else 1,
                           "settled_from": "vpsexec journal", "reports": {}})
        if rec.get("status") not in ("ok", "skipped"):
            if not u["read"] and _check_uncertain(u, run_id, rec.get("digest"), ask):
                u["done"], u["reports"] = "ok", {}
            continue
        if rec.get("digest") != u["digest"]:
            raise Refused(
                "%s step %d already %s in run %s with plan %s, but now plans as %s. "
                "The step changed under the run; resume will neither re-run a done "
                "step nor skip a changed one. Restore the play, or start a fresh run "
                "without --resume." % (_play_name(u["play"]), u["n"], rec["status"],
                                       run_id, str(rec.get("digest"))[:12], u["digest"][:12]))
        u["done"] = rec["status"]
        u["reports"] = dict(rec.get("reports") or {})
    return units


def _guard_only(rc, out):
    """The door refused, and the identical-plan guard is its only refusal."""
    return rc != 0 and GUARD_TEXT in out and out.count("REFUSED:") == 1


def own_repeat_wait(u, run_id, window=None):
    """(seconds to wait, None) when every attempt of this plan inside the
    door's window is THIS run's attempt at THIS step and this run's journal
    shows that step failed; otherwise (None, why). The door decides again
    after the wait; nothing here lifts its guard."""
    from vpscfg import vpsexec, vpsexeclog
    window = window or vpsexec.REPEAT_WINDOW_SECONDS
    reason = step_reason(u["play"], u["n"], u["step"], run_id)
    attempts = vpsexeclog.query(vpsexeclog.read(), plan_hash=u["digest"],
                                event="mutation_attempt", since_seconds=window + 5)
    if not attempts:
        return None, "the door's journal shows no attempt of this plan in its window"
    others = [a for a in attempts if a.get("reason") != reason]
    if others:
        return None, ("another run's identical plan ran inside the window (reason %r)"
                      % others[-1].get("reason"))
    dones = [r for r in _run_records(run_id) if r.get("event") == "step_done"
             and r.get("play") == _key(u["play"]) and r.get("step") == u["n"]]
    if not dones or dones[-1].get("status") != "failed" or dones[-1].get("digest") != u["digest"]:
        return None, "this run's journal does not show this step failing"
    age = vpsexeclog.age_seconds(attempts[-1])
    if age is None:
        return None, "the earlier attempt's timestamp is unreadable"
    return max(1, int(window - age) + 2), None


def _window():
    from vpscfg import vpsexec
    return vpsexec.REPEAT_WINDOW_SECONDS


def countdown(seconds, sleep):
    for left in range(seconds, 0, -1):
        sys.stdout.write("\r  repeat guard: retrying in %4ds  (Ctrl-C stops; --resume "
                         "continues later) " % left)
        sys.stdout.flush()
        sleep(1)
    print("\r  repeat guard: window passed — asking the door again.%s" % (" " * 30))


def _run_unit(u, run, run_id, contract, sleep):
    """(problem, rc, output) for one step. Reads go as plain reads."""
    argv = step_argv(u["play"], u["n"], u["step"], run_id)
    if u["read"]:
        # A plain read: the same argv a human would type, with no --run,
        # --approve or contract. Without --run the door executes nothing
        # that is not a read, so a step it judges otherwise ran nothing.
        rc, out = run(argv)
        print(printable(out.rstrip()))
        tier = TIER_RE.search(out)
        if rc == 0 and (tier is None or tier.group(1) != "read"):
            return "not-read", rc, out
        return None, rc, out
    extra = ["--approval-contract=" + contract] if u.get("bg") else []
    full = argv + ["--run", "--approve=" + u["digest"]] + extra
    rc, out = run(full)
    print(printable(out.rstrip()))
    if _guard_only(rc, out):
        wait, why = own_repeat_wait(u, run_id)
        if wait is None:
            print("  repeat guard: NOT retrying — %s." % why)
            print("  To continue: wait until %s (the door's %ds window), then "
                  "resume this run with --resume."
                  % (time.strftime("%H:%M", time.localtime(time.time() + _window() + 60)),
                     _window()))
        else:
            print("  repeat guard: the earlier identical attempt was this run's own "
                  "failed step; waiting out the door's window, then asking again.")
            countdown(wait, sleep)
            rc, out = run(full)
            print(printable(out.rstrip()))
    return None, rc, out


def _when_verdict(u, units):
    """True/False for a conditional step, or None when it cannot be known."""
    cond = u["step"]["when"]
    dep = [x for x in units if x["play"] is u["play"] and x["n"] == cond["step"]][0]
    if dep["done"] == "skipped":
        return False  # it did not run, so it reported nothing
    return dep["reports"].get(str(u["n"]))


def _reports(u, out):
    """For every later step conditioned on this one: did its regex match?"""
    if not u["step"].get("id"):
        return {}
    remote = remote_output(out)
    return dict((str(k), bool(re.search(s["when"]["regex"], remote)))
                for k, s in enumerate(u["play"]["steps"], 1)
                if s.get("when") and s["when"]["step"] == u["n"])


def _notify(ctx, event, **fields):
    send = ctx.get("notify")
    if send is None:
        from vpscfg import notify
        send = notify.send
    send(event, dict(fields, kind=ctx["kind"], name=ctx["name"], run_id=ctx["run_id"]))


def _where(ctx, u):
    if ctx["kind"] == "release":
        return "play %s step %d" % (_play_name(u["play"]), u["n"])
    return "step %d" % u["n"]


def _halt(ctx, u, rc, later, why=None, out=""):
    noun = ctx["kind"].upper()
    if why:
        print("\n%s HALTED at %s: %s %d later step(s) NOT run."
              % (noun, _where(ctx, u), why, later))
    else:
        print("\n%s HALTED at %s (rc=%s). %d later step(s) NOT run."
              % (noun, _where(ctx, u), rc, later))
    print("The agent can read what happened with: vpsexec last -n %d" % ctx["ran"])
    locked = []
    for host in RECONCILE_RE.findall(out or ""):
        if host not in locked:
            locked.append(host)
    for host in locked:
        print("A host lock is held on %s. Next, a human runs, in a terminal:\n"
              "  vpsexec reconcile %s" % (host, host))
    print("Resume this run (%s) after fixing the cause:\n  %s" % (ctx["run_id"], ctx["resume"]))
    offers = ctx.get("on_fail") or []
    if offers:
        print("Rollback — offered, NOT run (a human decides):")
        for o in offers:
            print("  %s" % o["command"])
    _rjournal({"event": "run_halted", "run_id": ctx["run_id"], "kind": ctx["kind"],
               "name": ctx["name"], "play": _key(u["play"]), "step": u["n"], "rc": rc})
    _notify(ctx, "halt", at=_where(ctx, u), rc=rc, resume=ctx["resume"],
            rollback=[o["command"] for o in offers])
    return rc


def _stop_at_boundary(ctx, pk, play, rc, why, extra=None):
    _rjournal(dict({"event": "run_halted", "run_id": ctx["run_id"], "kind": ctx["kind"],
                    "name": ctx["name"], "play": pk, "step": 0, "rc": rc}, **(extra or {})))
    print("%s %s before play %s — nothing of it ran. Continue with:\n  %s"
          % (ctx["kind"].upper(), why, _play_name(play), ctx["resume"]))
    _notify(ctx, "halt", at="before play %s" % _play_name(play), rc=rc,
            resume=ctx["resume"], rollback=[])
    return rc


def _replan_play(units, pk, play, ctx):
    """At a play boundary (and after its hold): plan the play again, because
    the plays before it changed live state since the release phrase. If any
    step now plans differently, show the new plans and ask a phrase bound to
    the NEW plan-hashes (M7); anything else stops here. Returns rc or None."""
    mine = [u for u in units if _key(u["play"]) == pk and not u["done"]]
    if not mine:
        return None
    fresh = dict((f["n"], f) for f in ctx["replan"](play))
    changed = [u for u in mine if not u["read"] and fresh[u["n"]]["digest"] != u["digest"]]
    if not changed:
        return None
    for u in changed:
        f = fresh[u["n"]]
        if bool(BREAK_GLASS_RE.search(f["text"])) != bool(BREAK_GLASS_RE.search(u["text"])):
            return _stop_at_boundary(ctx, pk, play, 2, "STOPPED (step %d changed break-glass "
                                     "status on re-plan; its grant was chosen for the old "
                                     "plan)" % u["n"])
    print("")
    print("RE-PLANNED play %s — %d step(s) now plan differently than when the release "
          "was approved (an earlier play changed the hosts):" % (_play_name(play),
                                                                  len(changed)))
    for u in changed:
        print("=" * 72)
        print("STEP %d — %s   (was plan %s, now %s)" % (u["n"], u["step"]["why"],
                                                       u["digest"][:12],
                                                       fresh[u["n"]]["digest"][:12]))
        print(printable(fresh[u["n"]]["text"].rstrip()))
    print("=" * 72)
    want = run_phrase("REPLAN:%s" % _play_name(play), [u["step"] for u in changed],
                      [fresh[u["n"]]["digest"] for u in changed])
    from vpscfg import vpsexecgrant
    vpsexecgrant.flush_input(ctx["stream"])
    if ctx["prompt"]("Type %s to run the new plans, anything else stops here: "
                     % want).strip() != want:
        return _stop_at_boundary(ctx, pk, play, 3, "STOPPED (new plans not approved)",
                                 {"replan": True})
    for u in changed:
        u["digest"], u["text"] = fresh[u["n"]]["digest"], fresh[u["n"]]["text"]
    _rjournal({"event": "play_replanned", "run_id": ctx["run_id"], "play": pk,
               "steps": [{"step": u["n"], "digest": u["digest"]} for u in changed]})
    return None


def execute_units(units, run, ctx):
    """Run every unit not already done, in order; halt on the first failure.
    With ctx["replan"] (a release), each play after the first one that runs is
    planned again at its boundary (after its hold) and changed plans are
    approved again before any of its steps run."""
    run_id, holds = ctx["run_id"], ctx.get("holds") or {}
    sleep = ctx.get("sleep") or time.sleep
    passed_hold, replanned = set(), set()
    total = len(units)
    ctx["ran"] = 0
    for i, u in enumerate(units):
        play, n, s = u["play"], u["n"], u["step"]
        pk = _key(play)
        hold = holds.get(pk)
        if hold and pk not in passed_hold and not any(
                x["done"] for x in units if _key(x["play"]) == pk):
            passed_hold.add(pk)
            want = "GO:%s" % _play_name(play)
            print("")
            print("HOLD before play %s — %s" % (_play_name(play), hold))
            from vpscfg import vpsexecgrant
            vpsexecgrant.flush_input(ctx["stream"])
            if ctx["prompt"]("Type %s to continue, anything else stops here: " % want
                             ).strip() != want:
                _rjournal({"event": "run_halted", "run_id": run_id, "kind": ctx["kind"],
                           "name": ctx["name"], "play": pk, "step": 0, "rc": 3,
                           "hold": True})
                print("%s HELD before play %s — nothing of it ran. Continue with:\n  %s"
                      % (ctx["kind"].upper(), _play_name(play), ctx["resume"]))
                return 3
        if ctx.get("replan") and pk not in replanned and ctx["ran"]:
            replanned.add(pk)
            stopped = _replan_play(units, pk, play, ctx)
            if stopped is not None:
                return stopped
        replanned.add(pk)
        print("")
        if ctx["kind"] == "release":
            print(">>> PLAY %s STEP %d of %d — %s"
                  % (_play_name(play), n, len(play["steps"]), s["why"]))
        else:
            print(">>> STEP %d of %d — %s" % (n, total, s["why"]))
        if u["done"]:
            print("    already %s in run %s — not run again"
                  % ("done" if u["done"] == "ok" else "skipped by its condition", run_id))
            continue
        later = sum(1 for x in units[i + 1:] if not x["done"])
        if s.get("when"):
            verdict = _when_verdict(u, units)
            if verdict is None:
                return _halt(ctx, u, 2, later,
                             why="its condition depends on step %d's output, which this "
                                 "run did not record." % s["when"]["step"])
            if not verdict:
                print("    SKIPPED: step %d (%s) did not report /%s/"
                      % (s["when"]["step"], s["when"]["id"], s["when"]["regex"]))
                _rjournal({"event": "step_done", "run_id": run_id, "play": pk, "step": n,
                           "digest": u["digest"], "status": "skipped",
                           "why": "condition not met: %s reports /%s/"
                                  % (s["when"]["id"], s["when"]["regex"])})
                u["done"] = "skipped"
                continue
        _rjournal({"event": "step_started", "run_id": run_id, "play": pk, "step": n,
                   "digest": u["digest"]})
        ctx["ran"] += 1
        problem, rc, out = _run_unit(u, run, run_id, ctx["contract"], sleep)
        u["reports"] = _reports(u, out)
        ok = rc == 0 and not problem
        _rjournal({"event": "step_done", "run_id": run_id, "play": pk, "step": n,
                   "digest": u["digest"], "status": "ok" if ok else "failed", "rc": rc,
                   "reports": u["reports"]})
        if "lock retained" in out.lower():
            _notify(ctx, "lock_retained", at=_where(ctx, u), rc=rc, resume=ctx["resume"])
        if problem == "not-read":
            return _halt(ctx, u, 2, later,
                         why="the door did not run it as a read (policy may classify "
                             "it differently) — nothing ran for it.")
        if not ok:
            return _halt(ctx, u, rc, later, out=out)
        u["done"] = "ok"
    _rjournal({"event": "run_complete", "run_id": run_id, "kind": ctx["kind"],
               "name": ctx["name"]})
    print("\n%s COMPLETE — %d step(s). The agent reads it with: vpsexec last -n %d"
          % (ctx["kind"].upper(), total, max(ctx["ran"], 1)))
    _notify(ctx, "finish", steps=total, ran=ctx["ran"])
    return 0


def _choose_grant(label, to_run, contract, load_grant, release=None):
    """One grant for every break-glass step that will run. Marks those units
    `bg` and returns (contract, picked, break-glass step numbers)."""
    combined = {"path": label, "steps": [u["step"] for u in to_run]}
    plans = [(u["text"], u["digest"]) for u in to_run]
    picked = None
    if contract in (None, AUTO):
        contract = None
        bg = [k for k, (text, _) in enumerate(plans, 1) if BREAK_GLASS_RE.search(text)]
        found = auto_pick(combined, plans, bg, release=release) if bg else None
        if found:
            contract, picked = found
    bg_steps = contract_coverage(combined, plans, contract, load_grant)
    for k, u in enumerate(to_run, 1):
        u["bg"] = k in bg_steps
    return contract, picked, bg_steps


BODY_LINE_RE = re.compile(r"^      ")
COLLAPSE_AFTER = 15


def _collapse_bodies(text, full):
    """An action step's body (docs/ACTIONS.md: "the full body... collapsed
    after 15 lines, --full expands") is what the plan-hash binds either way;
    collapsing here only shortens what scrolls past before approval."""
    if full:
        return text
    lines, out, i = text.splitlines(), [], 0
    while i < len(lines):
        out.append(lines[i])
        if lines[i] == "    body:":
            i += 1
            body = []
            while i < len(lines) and BODY_LINE_RE.match(lines[i]):
                body.append(lines[i])
                i += 1
            if len(body) > COLLAPSE_AFTER:
                out += body[:COLLAPSE_AFTER]
                out.append("      ... %d more line(s) — vpsrun --full shows the body "
                           "in full (the hash binds all of it either way)"
                           % (len(body) - COLLAPSE_AFTER))
            else:
                out += body
            continue
        i += 1
    return "\n".join(out)


def _show(units, ctx):
    full = ctx.get("full", False)
    for u in units:
        s = u["step"]
        print("=" * 72)
        if ctx["kind"] == "release":
            print("PLAY %s — STEP %d of %d — %s"
                  % (_play_name(u["play"]), u["n"], len(u["play"]["steps"]), s["why"]))
        else:
            print("STEP %d of %d — %s" % (u["n"], len(units), s["why"]))
        if u["done"]:
            print("ALREADY %s in run %s — will NOT run again (plan %s)"
                  % ("DONE" if u["done"] == "ok" else "SKIPPED", ctx["run_id"],
                     u["digest"][:12]))
            continue
        if s.get("when"):
            print("OPTIONAL — runs only if step %d (%s) reports /%s/; otherwise "
                  "skipped and journaled" % (s["when"]["step"], s["when"]["id"],
                                             s["when"]["regex"]))
        print(printable(_collapse_bodies(u["text"], full).rstrip()))
    print("=" * 72)


def _print_grant(contract, picked, bg_steps):
    if bg_steps:
        print("contract: %s covers break-glass step(s) %s"
              % (contract, ", ".join(map(str, bg_steps))))
    if picked:
        print("grant  : auto-picked %s %s  code %s  (expires %s)%s"
              % (picked["kind"], _short_id(picked["session_id"]), picked["code"],
                 picked["until"], "" if picked["left"] is None
                 else "  %d use(s) left" % picked["left"]))
        if picked["ties"]:
            print("         %d other grant(s) ranked equal (%s); picked the lowest "
                  "session id" % (len(picked["ties"]),
                                  ", ".join(_short_id(t) for t in picked["ties"])))


def _ask(prompt, stream, want, count):
    from vpscfg import vpsexecgrant
    vpsexecgrant.flush_input(stream)  # stray keys must not answer the prompt
    if prompt("Type %s to run all %d step(s) in order, anything else aborts: "
              % (want, count)).strip() != want:
        raise Refused("approval text did not match %r — nothing ran" % want)


def _asker(prompt, stream):
    """The TTY prompt resume uses to settle a reconciled step. One answer per
    question per invocation (a release re-plans after minting a grant)."""
    answers = {}

    def ask(msg):
        if msg not in answers:
            from vpscfg import vpsexecgrant
            vpsexecgrant.flush_input(stream)
            answers[msg] = prompt(msg)
        return answers[msg]
    return ask


def _operator():
    from vpscfg import vpsexecgrant
    return vpsexecgrant.operator()  # the password database, never $USER


def _require_tty(stream, what):
    if not (hasattr(stream, "isatty") and stream.isatty()):
        raise Refused("vpsrun needs a real terminal. It is how a HUMAN approves a "
                      "%s; open a terminal (not `!`) and run it there." % what)


def _grant_record(picked, bg_steps):
    return {"auto": True, "kind": picked["kind"], "session_id": picked["session_id"],
            "approval_code": picked["code"], "break_glass_steps": bg_steps}


def _start_run(kind, name, resume):
    """(run id, resumed). A new run is journaled only once it is approved, so
    an aborted approval leaves nothing for --resume to pick up."""
    if resume:
        return find_resumable(kind, name), True
    return new_run_id(), False


def _journal_start(kind, name, run_id, resumed, extra):
    _rjournal(dict({"event": "run_resumed" if resumed else "run_started",
                    "run_id": run_id, "kind": kind, "name": name}, **extra))


def run_play(play, run, prompt, stream, check=None, contract=None, load_grant=None,
             resume=False, sleep=None, notify=None, full=False):
    _require_tty(stream, "play")
    name = _key(play)
    run_id, resumed = _start_run("play", name, resume)
    units = prepare([play], run, run_id, check)
    if resumed:
        resume_plan(units, run_id, ask=_asker(prompt, stream))
    to_run = [u for u in units if not u["done"]]
    contract, picked, bg_steps = _choose_grant(play["path"], to_run, contract, load_grant)
    ctx = {"kind": "play", "name": name, "run_id": run_id, "contract": contract,
           "prompt": prompt, "stream": stream, "sleep": sleep, "notify": notify,
           "full": full, "resume": "vpsrun %s --resume" % shlex.quote(play["path"])}
    _show(units, ctx)
    print("play   : %s  (sha256 %s)" % (play["path"], play["sha256"][:16]))
    print("reason : %s" % play["reason"])
    print("run    : %s%s" % (run_id, "  (RESUMED — done steps are not run again)"
                             if resumed else ""))
    _print_grant(contract, picked, bg_steps)
    if not to_run:
        print("Nothing left to run in run %s." % run_id)
        if resumed:
            _rjournal({"event": "run_complete", "run_id": run_id, "kind": "play",
                       "name": name})
        return 0
    want = (phrase(play, [u["digest"] for u in units]) if not resumed
            else run_phrase("PLAY", [u["step"] for u in to_run],
                            [u["digest"] for u in to_run]))
    _ask(prompt, stream, want, len(to_run))
    _journal_start("play", name, run_id, resumed, {"play_sha256": play["sha256"]})

    from vpscfg import journal
    approved = {
        "event": "play_approved", "play": play["path"], "play_sha256": play["sha256"],
        "reason": play["reason"], "steps": [u["digest"] for u in to_run],
        "operator": _operator(), "run_id": run_id,
        "resumed": resumed}
    if picked:
        approved["grant"] = _grant_record(picked, bg_steps)
    journal.append("vpsexec", approved)
    return execute_units(units, run, ctx)


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# releases: releases/NAME.yaml — plays in order, one phrase
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

RELEASE_KEYS = {"version", "reason", "plays", "policies", "grant_ttl", "on_fail"}
RELEASE_ENTRY_KEYS = {"play", "hold_before"}
ON_FAIL_KEYS = {"runbook", "step"}
DEFAULT_GRANT_TTL = "12h"


def _named(what, name, directory):
    name = str(name)
    if not NAME_RE.match(name) or ".." in name:
        raise Refused("%s name %r: 1-64 of [A-Za-z0-9._-], starting with a letter or "
                      "digit (no paths)" % (what, name))
    return Path(directory) / (name if name.endswith((".yaml", ".yml")) else name + ".yaml")


def _rollback_offer(release_name, entry, n, policy_dir):
    """A rollback runbook entry, rendered as the exact vpsexec command to type.
    Printed when a release halts; never run by vpsrun."""
    import yaml
    from vpscfg.vpsexecpolicy import ROLLBACK_MARK
    if not isinstance(entry, dict) or set(entry) != ON_FAIL_KEYS:
        raise Refused("on_fail %d: exactly {runbook: <policy file>, step: <n>}" % n)
    path = _named("on_fail %d runbook" % n, entry["runbook"], policy_dir)
    if not path.exists():
        # An action policy lives in policies/actions/ (docs/ACTIONS.md); a
        # release names it by its bare file name, as _release_policy_paths reads.
        alt = _named("on_fail %d runbook" % n, entry["runbook"], Path(policy_dir) / "actions")
        if alt.exists():
            path = alt
    step = entry["step"]
    if isinstance(step, bool) or not isinstance(step, int) or step < 1:
        raise Refused("on_fail %d: step must be a runbook entry number (1-based)" % n)
    try:
        doc = yaml.safe_load(path.read_bytes())
    except (OSError, yaml.YAMLError) as e:
        raise Refused("on_fail %d: cannot read %s (%s)" % (n, path, e))
    books = (doc or {}).get("runbooks") if isinstance(doc, dict) else None
    if not isinstance(books, list) or step > len(books) or not isinstance(books[step - 1], dict):
        raise Refused("on_fail %d: %s has no runbook entry %d" % (n, path.name, step))
    rb = books[step - 1]
    if not (rb.get("rollback") is True or ROLLBACK_MARK in str(rb.get("why", "")).lower()):
        raise Refused("on_fail %d: %s entry %d is not a rollback entry (rollback: true)"
                      % (n, path.name, step))
    hosts = rb.get("hosts", rb.get("host"))
    hosts = [hosts] if isinstance(hosts, str) else hosts
    is_action = "action" in rb
    if not isinstance(hosts, list) or not hosts or not (
            is_action or str(rb.get("cmd") or "").strip()):
        raise Refused("on_fail %d: %s entry %d has no hosts or cmd" % (n, path.name, step))
    argv = ["vpsexec", ",".join(_clean("on_fail host", h) for h in hosts)]
    if is_action:
        with_value = rb.get("with") or {}
        if not isinstance(with_value, dict):
            raise Refused("on_fail %d: %s entry %d with: is not a mapping" % (n, path.name, step))
        argv += ["--action", _clean("on_fail action", rb["action"]),
                 "--with", _clean("on_fail with", json.dumps(with_value, sort_keys=True))]
    else:
        argv.append(_clean("on_fail cmd", rb["cmd"]))
    if rb.get("where") == "container":
        if not rb.get("container"):
            raise Refused("on_fail %d: %s entry %d runs in a container it does not name "
                          "— vpsrun cannot print an exact command for it" % (n, path.name, step))
        argv.append("--in=" + _clean("on_fail container", rb["container"]))
    if rb.get("break_glass"):
        argv.append("--break-glass")
    argv += ["--run", "--reason", "rollback after release %s halted" % release_name]
    return {"runbook": path.name, "step": step,
            "command": " ".join(shlex.quote(a) for a in argv)}


def load_release(name, release_dir=None, play_dir=None, policy_dir=None):
    import yaml
    from vpscfg import vpsexecgrant
    path = _named("release", name, release_dir or RELEASE_DIR)
    try:
        raw = path.read_bytes()
    except OSError as e:
        raise Refused("no release %s (%s)" % (path, e.strerror or e))
    doc = yaml.safe_load(raw)
    if not isinstance(doc, dict) or doc.get("version") != 1:
        raise Refused("%s: not a version-1 release" % path)
    unknown = sorted(set(doc) - RELEASE_KEYS)
    if unknown:
        raise Refused("%s: unknown key(s) %r" % (path, unknown))
    reason = _clean("release reason", doc.get("reason") or "").strip()
    if not reason:
        raise Refused("%s: a release needs a reason" % path)
    entries = doc.get("plays")
    if not isinstance(entries, list) or not entries:
        raise Refused("%s: plays must be a non-empty list" % path)
    plays, holds, seen = [], {}, set()
    for n, e in enumerate(entries, 1):
        if isinstance(e, str):
            e = {"play": e}
        if not isinstance(e, dict) or "play" not in e or set(e) - RELEASE_ENTRY_KEYS:
            raise Refused("%s: plays entry %d must be a play name or {play: NAME, "
                          "hold_before: \"what the human checks\"}" % (path, n))
        try:
            play = load_play(_named("play", e["play"], play_dir or PLAY_DIR))
        except OSError as err:
            raise Refused("%s: play %s: %s" % (path, e["play"], err.strerror or err))
        if _key(play) in seen:
            raise Refused("%s: play %s is listed twice — a release runs each play once"
                          % (path, e["play"]))
        seen.add(_key(play))
        if "hold_before" in e:
            hold = _clean("hold_before", e["hold_before"] or "").strip()
            if not hold:
                raise Refused("%s: hold_before on %s needs the question the human "
                              "answers" % (path, e["play"]))
            holds[_key(play)] = hold
        plays.append(play)
    policies = doc.get("policies") or []
    if not isinstance(policies, list) or not all(
            isinstance(p, str) and NAME_RE.match(p) for p in policies):
        raise Refused("%s: policies must be a list of policy file names" % path)
    ttl = str(doc.get("grant_ttl") or DEFAULT_GRANT_TTL)
    if ttl not in vpsexecgrant.REUSABLE_TTLS:
        raise Refused("%s: grant_ttl %r is not a reusable-grant TTL (%s)"
                      % (path, ttl, ", ".join(vpsexecgrant.REUSABLE_TTLS)))
    stem = path.stem
    pdir = policy_dir or _estate.current().policies
    on_fail = doc.get("on_fail") or []
    if not isinstance(on_fail, list):
        raise Refused("%s: on_fail must be a list" % path)
    offers = [_rollback_offer(stem, o, n, pdir) for n, o in enumerate(on_fail, 1)]
    return {"name": stem, "path": str(path), "sha256": hashlib.sha256(raw).hexdigest(),
            "reason": reason, "plays": plays, "holds": holds, "policies": policies,
            "grant_ttl": ttl, "on_fail": offers}


def bg_scope(to_run):
    """(hosts, count) of the break-glass steps that will run, as the door
    resolved each plan: a release mints a grant for exactly those (H4b)."""
    hosts, count = [], 0
    for u in to_run:
        if not BREAK_GLASS_RE.search(u["text"]):
            continue
        count += 1
        m = PLAN_HOSTS_RE.search(u["text"])
        for h in (m.group(1).split(",") if m else []):
            h = h.strip()
            if h and h not in hosts:
                hosts.append(h)
    return hosts, count


def mint_argv(release, hosts=None, uses=None):
    """The door's `grant new` for this release: its policies, narrowed to the
    hosts its break-glass steps reach and to one use per such step, bound to
    this release (only it auto-picks the grant) and revoked when it completes."""
    argv = ["grant", "new", ",".join(release["policies"]), "--kind", "reusable",
            "--ttl", release["grant_ttl"]]
    if hosts:
        argv += ["--hosts", ",".join(hosts)]
    if uses:
        argv += ["--max-uses", str(uses)]
    return argv + ["--for-release", release["name"], "--run"]


def _bound_ids(units, name):
    return set(sid for u in units for sid, info in door_grants(u["text"]).items()
               if info.get("release") == name)


def _revoke_release_grants(sids, name):
    """The run completed: the grants minted for it are spent, permanently."""
    from vpscfg import vpsexecgrant
    for sid in sorted(sids):
        vpsexecgrant.revoke(sid)
        print("grant  : %s revoked — release %s completed" % (_short_id(sid), name))


def _door_mint(argv):
    """The door's own `grant new`, on this terminal: it shows what the grant
    authorises and asks for ITS phrase. vpsrun mints nothing itself."""
    return subprocess.run(VPSEXEC + argv).returncode


def _release_policy_paths(release, policy_dir=None):
    pdir = policy_dir or _estate.current().policies
    out = []
    for name in release["policies"]:
        p = Path(pdir) / name
        if not p.exists():
            p = Path(pdir) / "actions" / name
        out.append(p)
    return out


def _gate_release(release, lint_fn, preflight_fn, policy_dir=None):
    """Lint on save (D10): `vpsrun release NAME` runs lint plus --index-only
    preflight on every policy before anything is planned. NO-GO refuses here,
    before any phrase; GO-WITH-WARNINGS prints and continues."""
    if not release["policies"]:
        return
    from vpscfg import releasenew
    paths = _release_policy_paths(release, policy_dir)
    rc, text = releasenew.gate(paths, lint_fn or releasenew.default_lint,
                               preflight_fn or releasenew.default_preflight_index_only)
    if rc == 2:
        raise Refused("release %s: NO-GO on lint/preflight — nothing was planned:\n%s"
                      % (release["name"], text))
    if rc == 1:
        print("GO-WITH-WARNINGS — release %s (continuing):\n%s" % (release["name"], text))


def run_release(release, run, prompt, stream, check=None, contract=None,
                load_grant=None, resume=False, sleep=None, notify=None, mint=None,
                full=False, lint_fn=None, preflight_fn=None, policy_dir=None,
                gate_release=False):
    """`gate_release=True` (the `vpsrun release NAME` CLI always passes it) is
    "lint on save" (D10): runs lint + --index-only preflight on every policy
    before anything is planned. NO-GO refuses here, before any phrase;
    GO-WITH-WARNINGS prints and continues. Default False keeps this a plain
    plan-and-run function for callers (and tests) that gate separately."""
    _require_tty(stream, "release")
    name = release["name"]
    label = "release %s" % name
    if gate_release:
        _gate_release(release, lint_fn, preflight_fn, policy_dir)
    run_id, resumed = _start_run("release", name, resume)
    ask = _asker(prompt, stream)

    def plan(prechecks=True):
        units = prepare(release["plays"], run, run_id, check, prechecks=prechecks)
        if resumed:
            resume_plan(units, run_id, ask=ask)
        return units

    units = plan()
    to_run = [u for u in units if not u["done"]]
    needs_grant = contract in (None, AUTO) and any(
        BREAK_GLASS_RE.search(u["text"]) for u in to_run)
    if needs_grant and not auto_pick(
            {"path": label, "steps": [u["step"] for u in to_run]},
            [(u["text"], u["digest"]) for u in to_run],
            [k for k, u in enumerate(to_run, 1) if BREAK_GLASS_RE.search(u["text"])],
            release=name):
        hosts, uses = bg_scope(to_run)
        argv = mint_argv(release, hosts, uses)
        cmd = "vpsexec %s" % " ".join(shlex.quote(a) for a in (
            argv if release["policies"]
            else ["grant", "new", "<policy,...>", "--kind", "reusable", "--ttl",
                  release["grant_ttl"], "--run"]))
        if not release["policies"]:
            raise Refused("this release has break-glass steps and no valid grant covers "
                          "them all. Mint one reusable grant (%s), then re-run: vpsrun "
                          "release %s. Nothing was run." % (cmd, name))
        print("No valid grant covers this release's break-glass steps. Minting ONE "
              "reusable grant through the door:\n  %s" % cmd)
        print("The door shows what it authorises and asks for its own phrase; "
              "anything else aborts and nothing runs.")
        rc = (mint or _door_mint)(argv)
        if rc != 0:
            raise Refused("the grant was not minted (rc=%s) — nothing ran" % rc)
        units = plan(prechecks=False)  # the door lists the new grant per plan
        to_run = [u for u in units if not u["done"]]
    contract, picked, bg_steps = _choose_grant(label, to_run, contract, load_grant,
                                               release=name)
    # Revoked when the run completes: every grant bound to this release that
    # the door lists for its plans (the one just minted, or one from an earlier
    # attempt this --resume picked up).
    bound = _bound_ids(to_run, name)
    ctx = {"kind": "release", "name": name, "run_id": run_id, "contract": contract,
           "prompt": prompt, "stream": stream, "sleep": sleep, "notify": notify,
           "full": full, "holds": release["holds"], "on_fail": release["on_fail"],
           "resume": "vpsrun release %s --resume" % name}
    _show(units, ctx)
    print("release: %s  (sha256 %s)" % (release["path"], release["sha256"][:16]))
    print("reason : %s" % release["reason"])
    print("plays  : %s" % ", ".join(
        "%s%s" % (_play_name(p), " (HOLD before)" if _key(p) in release["holds"] else "")
        for p in release["plays"]))
    print("run    : %s%s" % (run_id, "  (RESUMED — done steps are not run again)"
                             if resumed else ""))
    _print_grant(contract, picked, bg_steps)
    if not to_run:
        print("Nothing left to run in run %s." % run_id)
        if resumed:
            _rjournal({"event": "run_complete", "run_id": run_id, "kind": "release",
                       "name": name})
        return 0
    want = run_phrase("RELEASE:%s" % name, [u["step"] for u in to_run],
                      [u["digest"] for u in to_run])
    _ask(prompt, stream, want, len(to_run))
    _journal_start("release", name, run_id, resumed, {
        "release_sha256": release["sha256"], "plays": [_key(p) for p in release["plays"]]})

    from vpscfg import journal
    approved = {"event": "release_approved", "release": release["path"],
                "release_sha256": release["sha256"], "reason": release["reason"],
                "run_id": run_id, "resumed": resumed,
                "plays": [{"play": u["play"]["path"], "play_sha256": u["play"]["sha256"],
                           "step": u["n"], "plan": u["digest"]} for u in to_run],
                "operator": _operator()}
    if picked:
        approved["grant"] = _grant_record(picked, bg_steps)
    journal.append("vpsexec", approved)
    ctx["replan"] = lambda play: prepare([play], run, run_id, check, prechecks=False)
    rc = execute_units(units, run, ctx)
    if rc == 0 and bound:
        _revoke_release_grants(bound, name)
    return rc


def release_check(name, lint_fn=None, preflight_fn=None, policy_dir=None,
                  release_dir=None, play_dir=None):
    """`vpsrun release check NAME` = lint + full (live-capable) preflight,
    read-only. Safe for the agent to run: it never plans or approves a step."""
    from vpscfg import releasenew
    release = load_release(name, release_dir, play_dir, policy_dir)
    paths = _release_policy_paths(release, policy_dir)
    rc, text = releasenew.gate(paths, lint_fn or releasenew.default_lint,
                               preflight_fn or releasenew.default_preflight_live)
    print(text)
    print("VERDICT: %s" % releasenew.VERDICT_NAME[rc])
    return rc


def _vpscfg_run(argv):
    r = subprocess.run(VPSCFG + argv, capture_output=True, text=True)
    return r.returncode, r.stdout + r.stderr


PROGRESS_EVERY = 15  # seconds between "still running" lines for a long step


def _subprocess_run(argv, popen=None, clock=time.monotonic, err=None,
                    every=PROGRESS_EVERY):
    """The door, as a child. A step that takes longer than `every` seconds
    prints a "still running" line with its elapsed time (L8), so a long
    recreate is visibly alive; the door's full output follows when it ends."""
    p = (popen or subprocess.Popen)(VPSEXEC + argv, stdout=subprocess.PIPE,
                                    stderr=subprocess.PIPE, text=True)
    err = err or sys.stderr
    start = clock()
    while True:
        try:
            out, errs = p.communicate(timeout=every)
            break
        except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
            err.write("  ... still running (%ds) — %s\n"
                      % (int(clock() - start), " ".join(argv[:2])[:80]))
            err.flush()
    return p.returncode, (out or "") + (errs or "")


def parse_argv(argv):
    """`PLAY [--approval-contract[=]FILE|auto]` (alias `--grant`) -> (play path,
    absolute contract, AUTO, or None). None and AUTO both auto-pick."""
    positional, contract, i = [], None, 0
    while i < len(argv):
        a = argv[i]
        flag = a.split("=", 1)[0]
        if flag in ("--approval-contract", "--grant") and "=" in a:
            contract = a.split("=", 1)[1]
        elif a in ("--approval-contract", "--grant"):
            if i + 1 >= len(argv):
                raise Refused("--approval-contract needs a file path")
            contract = argv[i + 1]
            i += 1
        elif a.startswith("-"):
            raise Refused("unknown flag %r" % a)
        else:
            positional.append(a)
        i += 1
    if len(positional) != 1:
        raise Refused("usage: vpsrun PLAY.yaml [--approval-contract=FILE]")
    if contract is not None:
        if not contract.strip():
            raise Refused("--approval-contract needs a file path")
        if contract.strip() == AUTO:
            return positional[0], AUTO
        contract = os.path.abspath(os.path.expanduser(contract))
    return positional[0], contract


def parse_cli(argv):
    """`[release] TARGET [--resume] [--approval-contract=FILE|auto]` ->
    (mode, target, contract, resume)."""
    mode = "play"
    if len(argv) > 1 and argv[0] == "release":
        mode, argv = "release", argv[1:]
    resume = "--resume" in argv
    target, contract = parse_argv([a for a in argv if a != "--resume"])
    return mode, target, contract, resume


def parse_release_new_argv(argv):
    """`release new NAME --from POLICY[,POLICY...] [--replace]` ->
    (name, from_arg, replace)."""
    positional, from_arg, replace, i = [], None, False, 0
    while i < len(argv):
        a = argv[i]
        if a.startswith("--from="):
            from_arg = a.split("=", 1)[1]
        elif a == "--from":
            if i + 1 >= len(argv):
                raise Refused("--from needs a policy.yaml[,policy.yaml...]")
            from_arg = argv[i + 1]
            i += 1
        elif a == "--replace":
            replace = True
        elif a.startswith("-"):
            raise Refused("unknown flag %r" % a)
        else:
            positional.append(a)
        i += 1
    if len(positional) != 1 or not from_arg:
        raise Refused("usage: vpsrun release new NAME --from "
                      "policy.yaml[,policy.yaml...] [--replace]")
    return positional[0], from_arg, replace


def main(argv):
    if not argv or argv[0] in ("-h", "--help", "help"):
        queued = sorted(PLAY_DIR.glob("*.yaml")) if PLAY_DIR.is_dir() else []
        releases = sorted(RELEASE_DIR.glob("*.yaml")) if RELEASE_DIR.is_dir() else []
        print(__doc__.split("\n\n")[0])
        print("\n  vpsrun plays/NAME.yaml     show every step, type one phrase, run")
        print("                             break-glass steps: a valid grant covering")
        print("                             all of them is auto-picked from ~/.vpscfg/grants")
        print("  vpsrun plays/NAME.yaml --approval-contract=FILE")
        print("                             or name one grant yourself")
        print("  vpsrun release NAME        every play in releases/NAME.yaml, one phrase")
        print("  ... --resume               continue the latest unfinished run: steps")
        print("                             that already succeeded are not run again")
        print("  ... --full                 show every action step's body in full "
              "(plan review collapses it after 15 lines)")
        print("  vpsrun release new NAME --from policy.yaml[,policy.yaml...] [--replace]")
        print("                             scaffold plays/ and releases/ from a runbook; "
              "writes nothing under policies/, mints nothing, never --run")
        print("  vpsrun release check NAME  lint + full preflight, read-only")
        print("\nQueued plays:" if queued else "\nNo plays queued in plays/.")
        for p in queued:
            print("  %s" % p.relative_to(PLAY_DIR.parent))  # the estate root, not REPO
        if releases:
            print("\nReleases:")
            for p in releases:
                print("  vpsrun release %s" % p.stem)
        return 0
    from vpscfg import gates, releasenew
    mode, target = "play", None
    try:
        if len(argv) > 1 and argv[0] == "release" and argv[1] == "new":
            name, from_arg, replace = parse_release_new_argv(argv[2:])
            mode, target = "release-new", name
            result = releasenew.new(name, from_arg, replace=replace)
            for p in result["plays"]:
                print("play    : %s" % p)
            print("release : %s" % result["release"])
            print(result["report"])
            print("VERDICT: %s" % result["verdict"])
            return result["exit_code"]
        if len(argv) > 1 and argv[0] == "release" and argv[1] == "check":
            if len(argv) != 3:
                raise Refused("usage: vpsrun release check NAME")
            mode, target = "release-check", argv[2]
            return release_check(target)
        full = "--full" in argv
        mode, target, contract, resume = parse_cli([a for a in argv if a != "--full"])
        if mode == "release":
            return run_release(load_release(target), _subprocess_run,
                               lambda msg: input(msg), sys.stdin, contract=contract,
                               resume=resume, full=full, gate_release=True)
        return run_play(load_play(target), _subprocess_run,
                        lambda msg: input(msg), sys.stdin, contract=contract,
                        resume=resume, full=full)
    except (Refused, gates.Refused) as r:
        print("REFUSED: %s" % r, file=sys.stderr)
        _notify_outside_run("refused", mode, target, why=str(r))
        return 2
    except (KeyboardInterrupt, EOFError):
        print("\naborted — nothing further ran. An unfinished run continues with "
              "--resume.", file=sys.stderr)
        _notify_outside_run("aborted", mode, target)
        return 130


def _notify_outside_run(event, mode, target, why=None, send=None):
    """A refusal (planning, approval, resume) or a Ctrl-C reaches the human
    too (L8). The reason travels as its first line only, masked: never the
    door's plan or output."""
    from vpscfg import notify, secretmask
    fields = {"kind": mode, "name": str(target)[:200] if target else None}
    if why:
        first = (why.strip().splitlines() or [""])[0]
        fields["why"] = secretmask.mask(first)[:300]
    try:
        (send or notify.send)(event, fields)
    except Exception:  # a notifier never changes the exit status
        pass


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main(sys.argv[1:]))
